    "authoredBasis": "New written-mathematics choice diagram, not a recovered scan. Asset ID: choice-graph-pair-a.\nCorrect pair; both panels use y=6/x with its two branches.\n6/x=x-1 -> x^2-x-6=0 -> x=-2,3. 6/x=x+3 -> x^2+3x-6=0 -> x=(-3+-sqrt(33))/2. All roots are nonzero and determine the listed y coordinates.\nDeclared actual panel geometry: [{\"panel\":\"I\",\"curves\":[\"y=6/x\",\"y=x-1\"],\"intersections_exact\":[\"(-2,-3)\",\"(3,2)\"],\"intersection_x_labels\":[\"-2\",\"3\"],\"line_window_endpoints\":[[-6,-7],[6,5]]},{\"panel\":\"II\",\"curves\":[\"y=6/x\",\"y=x+3\"],\"intersections_exact\":[\"((-3-sqrt(33))/2,(3-sqrt(33))/2)\",\"((-3+sqrt(33))/2,(3+sqrt(33))/2)\"],\"intersections_numeric\":[[-4.372281323269014,-1.3722813232690143],[1.3722813232690143,4.372281323269014]],\"intersection_x_labels\":[\"-4.372\",\"1.372\"],\"line_window_endpoints\":[[-6,-3],[5,8]]}]\nEquation labels are uniformly omitted as a task-fidelity design: the stem supplies target equations, so learners must inspect graphs rather than match printed alternative formulas. This does not change source data or seek new human approval.\nSeparate reciprocal branches; x=0 is excluded mathematically. Algebraic window clipping is not a domain endpoint declaration. Segment approximation max error at 640 px: 0.037037037037037035 px.\nCurrent executable contract has no pointOnFunction/intersection/root-completeness assertion or analytic function object. Supported displacement/pointOnLine assertions must not be described as proving these unsupported constraints.",
